65:| Q68 | 04 EidCallback / Verifying leave the callback page, but don't say (a) what happens when neither stored context nor the query holds a valid market/locale pair (Q61), (b) which page runs the Gate after Verifying with `reviewStep` off (no Gate route in 08 Routes), (c) `plan_id` for `identity_started`/`identity_completed` when the context has no plan. | Frontend | (a) Callback replaces itself with `/` (root picks a language), no eID message: there is no locale to write it in. (b) Gate exit (reviewStep off) = Plans page `/{market}/{locale}/?plan=…&rungate=1`. `rungate=1` is a one-time marker: the Plans page (W-10, not built here) reads it once, runs the Gate, and strips it with `history.replaceState`, so a reload or Back shows Plans or the retry point and never runs the Gate automatically (04 invariant 1). W-09 only builds the URL (`exitUrl`). Every exit uses `location.replace` and carries plan and `utm_*` in the query. Review exit = `/{market}/{locale}/review/?plan=…`. (c) `plan_id: 'unknown'`, like `trial: 'unknown'` (07). |
66-| Q69 | 04 invariant 6 vs StartingEid: Back from the eID provider restores the page from the bfcache in StartingEid ("Opening …", no exit). Re-running the POST and redirect would trap Back. | Frontend | On `pageshow` with `persisted` while in StartingEid: no new POST. On the Plans page → Plans (cards back). On the callback page (Start again / Try again) → EidFailed(expired), which has Try again and Change plan. The redirect from the callback page uses `location.replace`, so `/auth/callback` never stays in history (04 EidCallback). |
67-| Q70 | 04 Terms / Gate (W-10): (a) where the Plans page gets the chosen plan and `?notice=` on a fresh load (return from another page), (b) how the Gate sees an order another tab wrote after load, (c) what "preselected" means on the retry point. | Frontend | (a) Plan = stored context, else `?plan=` (inv. 2); notice = `?notice=`, read once on reaching Plans, removed with `history.replaceState`, unknown value ignored. Plans shows the banner for any notice; Try again only when `reviewStep` is off, a plan is known and the notice is not `plan_unavailable`. (b) Plans/Review re-read the open order from `localStorage` right before Select / Try again / Pay and put its id in the context (`openOrderSynced`), so Gate step 1 sees it. (c) Retry point shows the banner and the chosen plan's title above the cards, plus Try again; cards stay selectable (= Change plan). `Resume` is a screen of its own, not a banner. The open order stores `{orderId, paymentUrl, planId, market, locale, snapshot{value, tax, currency, trial}}`; `saveOpenOrder` is run by CreatingOrder (W-11). |
68-
69-## P2: quality and non-functional
70-
71-| ID | Question | Owner | Working assumption |
72-|---|---|---|---|
73-| Q20 | Analytics: no dedupe rule for `purchase` (reload, repeated polling), no params for other events, no UTM storage spec. | Marketing | `purchase` fires once per `orderId` (localStorage guard, shared across tabs, written only after consent; see 07). All events carry `market`, `locale`, `review_step`, UTMs; `plan_id` where known. UTMs carried with the flow (see Q5, Q7). |
74-| Q21 | No accessibility requirement. Provider pages are outside our control. | Product | WCAG 2.2 AA for our pages. European Accessibility Act applies (EN 301 549 = WCAG 2.1 AA, included in 2.2 AA). |
75-| Q22 | "Under two minutes" and "70% on phones" have no metric or performance budget. | Product | Measure `plan_viewed` → `purchase` time. LCP < 2.5 s, INP < 200 ms (lab: TBT < 200 ms), CLS < 0.1 on mid-range mobile. JS ≤ 230 KB gzip on the plan page (raised from 150, then 200, Q54). |
76-| Q23 | Static CDN build vs prices: are prices baked in at build or fetched at runtime? | Backend + Platform | Plans fetched at build for first paint, re-fetched at runtime before Review. Review price is binding. |
77-| Q24 | Brief: 4 languages. Fixtures: local + `en` per market only. Is every language available in every market? Russian? | Product + Marketing | Local + `en` per market, as in the fixtures. |
